    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "57d70d5f31261d277c0a3daad3a78d3963f5a98a5daeb624c14ec65e9ad7f1e5",
      "text": "Private Transfer Mérida to Chichén Itzá and Shared Day Tour\n\nDuration: Full Day\n\nPick-Up: 9:00 – 9:30 AM\n\nLanguages: English and Spanish\n\nYour day begins with a private transfer from Mérida to Chichén Itzá, one of the most famous archaeological sites in the world and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Upon arrival, join a shared guided tour to explore the site’s most remarkable landmarks, including the iconic Temple of Kukulkán, the mysterious Sacred Cenote, and the impressive Great Ball Court, one of the largest ever built in Mesoamerica.\n\nAfter exploring the ruins, cool off with a refreshing swim in a nearby cenote, followed by a traditional Yucatecan lunch featuring regional flavors.\n\nThe journey continues with a stop in the charming colonial town of Valladolid, where you can stroll through colorful streets, admire historic architecture, and experience the relaxed atmosphere of this picturesque town.\n\nFinally, travel onward to the Riviera Maya, where you will be dropped off in Cancún, Playa del Carmen, or Tulum town. (Drop-off in Tulum hotel zone and Bahía Petempich is not included.)\n\nOnce you arrive, the rest of your Caribbean stay is yours to enjoy—relax on the beach or inquire about optional extensions to continue your adventure.\n\nIncluded:• Transportation• Guided tour at Chichén Itzá• Entrance fees• Lunch• Cenote visit• Drop-off in Riviera Maya\n\nNot Included:• Tips• Personal expenses• Overnight stay in Riviera Maya (optional)",
      "provenance": {
